<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>To Kill The Queen, 2022 - Western Version</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;FONT size=3 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=""&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;To Kill the Queen, 2022&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;USN/Western Human Player Version&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Al "Beirutdude" Sandrik&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;The Time Is: 15 April, 2022, 16:00 Zulu/01:00 Okinawa Time&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;First Island Chain/Ryukyu/Daito Islands&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable as West/USN Only&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;32 Hours Duration&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Background: Ten days ago, PLAN Marines landed on the Senkaku and Yaeyama Islands (The remotest part of Japan, and the last of the Ryukyu Islands near Taiwan). The rational was to deny the USN and JMSDF antisubmarine bases to interdict PLAN submarines from transiting into the Pacific through the First Island Chain. This was necessary as a prelude to isolating and invading the lost providence of Taiwan. The recently established Japanese garrison on Yonaguni Island put up a stubborn defense allowing time for USAF and JASDF squadrons from Okinawa to intervene. Subsequently, massive PLA Rocket Force barrages and persistent PLAAF airstrikes, with cratering munitions, have heavily damaged the three airbases on Okinawa leading to the withdrawal of the remaining U.S. and Japanese squadrons and isolation of the island from resupply. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;U.S. Marines and Japanese Ground Self Defense Forces are digging in for combined PRC airborne and amphibious assault on the island. To stiffen the defense Carrier Strike Group - Five has been dispatched to provide air support to the defenders. Realizing the CSG would likely be fighting for its life, the ships were heavily armed with every available ABM SAM in the Pacific Fleet’s inventory. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The USS Ronald Reagan is your "High Value Unit" (HVU) and the "Queen" on the chessboard. She SHOULD BE defended by an Inner Ring of Ticonderoga and Arleigh Burke Class Aegis missile CRUisers and DEStroyers (CRUDES) within 15 nm or so. An outer ring of CRUDES positioned 15 to 25 nm from the HVU to provide ASW and AAW support along the "Threat Axis" and a more distant "Picket" providing distant support and some additional radar coverage. Of course, it’s your scenario to play so good luck commander!&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Mission: You are to maintain patrol from a position east of the Ryukyu Islands, in the vicinity of the Daito Islands, providing Combat Air Patrol (CAP) over Okinawa in support of the Marines and Japanese Ground Self Defense Forces (JGSDF). You will need to maintain the USS Ronald Reagan within the CSG-5 OPAREA Box for 24 hours to claim victory. Damage to the carrier will result in negative Victory Points, and her sinking would constitute an outright disaster for the USN. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Notes:&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;1. You must run the scenario for about 5 seconds before you do anything else to allow PRC/PLAN vessels to Teleport. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;2. As of November, 2020 the combined PLAN/AF H-6 Inventory (of all variants) is estimated to be 231 aircraft, about 2/3s of them appear in this scenario (with a 20-30 percent maintenance downtime for each squadron). So, it may appear that there are a LOT of H-6s coming at you, well the PRC is building them like mad.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;3. You don’t get to play the PRC side in this version, there is a separate scenario for that role. As the Western/USN player can you keep the PRC/PLA(N)AF/PLAAF/PLA Rocket Forces from penetrating your carrier screen?&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;4. I have built up the PLAAF/PLA(N)AF Eastern Theater air bases for possible future use. So, if you look them over don’t panic, I do not use all of the aircraft in this scenario for the AI.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;5. The weather will randomly change, poising a challange for PRC recon and satellite assets.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Finally, unlike many of my scenarios, you don’t get points for every unit destroyed. The world is at war and the two titans of the Pacific are facing off. Unfortunately, lots of people are going to die, whether the public/politicians like it or not! In this case, you only loose points for damaging and/or destroying the HVU/carrier and only gain points by remaining on station for 12 hours (within the TF-70/CSG-5 OPAREA). The more damage inflicted on the USS Reagan the more points you lose.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Scoring: -6,000 points = Disaster and +6,000 = a Triumph&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Created with C:MO Build 1147.14&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;.INI and Delta Files are provided for deep rebuilds.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Al "BeirutDude" Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;/P&gt;&lt;U&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=blue&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
